---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";

export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Education & study · A2 Vocabulary",
  "slug": "education-and-study",
  "level": "A2",
  "topic": "Education & study",
  "category": "Vocabulary & Topics",
  "contentType": "vocabulary",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Describe a learning path, distinguish education words and study actions, report evidence of progress, and ask precise classroom questions.",
  "sequence": 17,
  "prerequisites": ["a1/present-simple", "a2/past-simple", "a2/present-perfect", "a2/verb-infinitive-ing"],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": ["a2-exit"],
  "tutorReviewRequired": true,
  "qualityReview": {
    "status": "editorial-review",
    "generatedPedagogy": true,
    "learnerPilotCount": 0,
    "scoredItemCount": 49,
    "revisionSummary": "Learning-path nouns, action-result contrasts, teach-learn-study-practice meaning, progress evidence, classroom repair, spoken form, listening, privacy, production, and retrieval were audited; three pilots remain."
  }
});
---

<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="50–60 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson {page.sequence}</p>
  <h1>Education &amp; study: <em>show what changed</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A useful learning update does more than name a school subject. It identifies the goal, course or class, study action, evidence of progress, current difficulty, and next step. Precise education words help another person understand what you are learning and what support you need.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">50–60 min core</span>
    <span class="tag">subject · course · class · program</span>
    <span class="tag">study · learn · teach · practice</span>
    <span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Find six information jobs in one learning update.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Separate the learning path, action, and result.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Choose precise education chunks and questions.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Give a fictional progress update with evidence.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish a subject, course, class, lesson, program, and qualification; distinguish registering, attending, taking, completing, and passing; use homework, assignment, exam, score, grade, and feedback accurately; separate study, learn, teach, practice, and review; report specific evidence of progress; ask for the exact clarification you need; and give a privacy-safe learning update.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a continuing present-perfect activity, a finished past action, and a planned infinitive.">
    <h3>Three earlier patterns</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Use present perfect with <span class="ex">since May</span>, past simple with <span class="ex">yesterday</span>, and an infinitive after <span class="ex">plans</span>.</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Earlier pattern choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="has studied">has studied</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="reviewed">reviewed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="to practice">to practice</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="studied">studied</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="reviews">reviews</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="practicing">practicing</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The course began in May and continues now: Leo <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="has studied" data-hint="Use has plus the past participle for an activity continuing from May to now." data-fix="Leo has studied workplace English since May.">choose</button> workplace English since May.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The action finished yesterday: He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="reviewed" data-hint="Use past simple because yesterday locates a finished review." data-fix="He reviewed his notes yesterday.">choose</button> his notes yesterday.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The verb after <span class="ex">plans</span> needs <span class="ex">to</span>: He plans <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="to practice" data-hint="Use the to-infinitive after plans." data-fix="He plans to practice one presentation tonight.">choose</button> one presentation tonight.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice six jobs in one learning update</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Harbor Communication update</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“My <strong>goal is to give clearer project updates</strong>. This semester, I’m taking <strong>Business English 2, one course in the Harbor Communication Certificate program</strong>. I <strong>attend the Tuesday class, review my notes, and practice one update after each lesson</strong>. Last month I needed four prompts; today <strong>I gave the same type of update with one prompt</strong>. I still <strong>need help answering follow-up questions</strong>, so I’m going to <strong>ask the tutor for another example</strong>.”</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Which phrase gives the goal? Which phrase locates the course inside a program?</li>
      <li>Which parts give the routine, progress evidence, current gap, and next step?</li>
      <li>Does the learner claim to be perfect, or give limited evidence of one change?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You identified the goal, course and program, study routine, progress evidence, current gap, and next step.">
    <h3>Discovery check: identify each information job</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Learning update choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="learning goal">learning goal</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="course and program">course and program</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="study routine">study routine</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="progress evidence">progress evidence</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="current gap">current gap</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="next step">next step</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">Give clearer project updates</span> states the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="learning goal" data-hint="The phrase names what the learner wants to be able to do." data-fix="Give clearer project updates states the learning goal.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">Business English 2 in the Harbor Communication Certificate</span> states the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="course and program" data-hint="One named course belongs to a larger organized set of courses." data-fix="Business English 2 and the Harbor Communication Certificate state the course and program.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Attending, reviewing, and practicing after each lesson give the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="study routine" data-hint="These repeated actions show how the learner works between lessons." data-fix="Attending, reviewing, and practicing give the study routine.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The change from four prompts to one prompt gives <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="progress evidence" data-hint="The before-and-now comparison shows a specific change in performance." data-fix="Four prompts before and one prompt now provide progress evidence.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Needing help with follow-up questions gives the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="current gap" data-hint="The learner names the part that still needs work." data-fix="Answering follow-up questions is the current gap.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Asking the tutor for another example gives the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="next step" data-hint="This is the specific action planned after identifying the gap." data-fix="Asking for another example is the next step.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: locate each word on the learning path</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Education systems use some labels differently. Instead of memorizing one universal school path, identify the job the word does in the current context.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>word</th><th>job</th><th>fictional Harbor example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">subject</span></td><td>an area of knowledge or skill</td><td><span class="ex">Business English is the subject.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">course</span></td><td>an organized series of study with goals or requirements</td><td><span class="ex">Business English 2 is a twelve-week course.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">class</span></td><td>a scheduled meeting, group, or course in everyday U.S. English</td><td><span class="ex">The Tuesday class starts at 6:00.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">lesson</span></td><td>one teaching unit or focus</td><td><span class="ex">Today’s lesson focuses on project updates.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">program</span></td><td>an organized set of related courses or activities</td><td><span class="ex">The certificate program contains three courses.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">qualification</span></td><td>a recognized result showing that requirements were completed</td><td><span class="ex">The certificate is the program’s qualification.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Certificate, diploma</span>, and <span class="ex">degree</span> are not automatic synonyms. Their level, length, and official meaning depend on the institution and education system. Use the exact name on the fictional or official document.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated the area of study, organized course, scheduled class, teaching unit, multi-course program, and recognized qualification.">
    <h3>Drill 1: choose the learning-path noun</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Learning-path noun choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="subject">subject</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="course">course</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="class">class</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="lesson">lesson</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="program">program</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="qualification">qualification</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The learner is interested in the general field of workplace English. Workplace English is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="subject" data-hint="Choose the word for the area of knowledge or skill." data-fix="Workplace English is the subject.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Business English 2 has twelve weeks, stated goals, and four assignments. It is a <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="course" data-hint="Choose the organized series of study with its own goals and requirements." data-fix="Business English 2 is a twelve-week course.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The group meets every Tuesday at 6:00. The scheduled Tuesday meeting is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="class" data-hint="Choose the everyday U.S. word for the scheduled meeting." data-fix="The scheduled Tuesday meeting is the class.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Today’s teaching unit focuses only on asking follow-up questions. That unit is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="lesson" data-hint="Choose the word for one teaching unit or focus." data-fix="Today’s unit on follow-up questions is the lesson.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The Harbor Communication Certificate contains three related courses. The complete three-course set is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="program" data-hint="Choose the word for the organized set of related courses." data-fix="The three-course set is the program.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>After meeting every stated requirement, the learner receives a recognized certificate. In this context, the certificate is the <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="qualification" data-hint="Choose the general word for a recognized result after requirements are met." data-fix="The recognized certificate is the qualification in this fictional program.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep enrollment, participation, and results distinct</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>stage</th><th>useful chunks</th><th>what the chunk does and does not say</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>join</td><td><span class="ex">sign up for / register for / enroll in a course</span></td><td>become an official participant; the exact administrative word varies</td></tr>
      <tr><td>participate</td><td><span class="ex">take a course · attend class</span></td><td><span class="ex">take</span> presents participation; <span class="ex">attend</span> means be present</td></tr>
      <tr><td>do the work</td><td><span class="ex">do homework · complete / submit an assignment · study for an exam</span></td><td><span class="ex">homework</span> is normally noncount; <span class="ex">assignment</span> is countable</td></tr>
      <tr><td>be assessed</td><td><span class="ex">take an exam · get a score, grade, or feedback</span></td><td>taking an exam does not state its result</td></tr>
      <tr><td>finish or succeed</td><td><span class="ex">complete a course · pass a course / exam</span></td><td>completing requirements and meeting the required standard are different ideas</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>A <span class="ex">score</span> often gives points or a percentage. A <span class="ex">grade</span> may be a letter, band, number, or overall course result. <span class="ex">Feedback</span> gives comments about what works and what to improve. Systems vary, so the context should state which one it means.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished registration, attendance, submission, taking an exam, passing a course, and receiving feedback by their actual result.">
    <h3>Drill 2: choose the exact education action</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Education action choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="registered for">registered for</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="attended">attended</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="submitted">submitted</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="took">took</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="passed">passed</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="received">received</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Leo completed the official online form and now has a place in Business English 2: He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="registered for" data-hint="The completed official form made Leo a participant in the course." data-fix="Leo registered for Business English 2.">choose</button> Business English 2.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Maya was present from the beginning to the end of Tuesday’s scheduled meeting: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="attended" data-hint="Attend reports presence at the scheduled class." data-fix="Maya attended Tuesday’s class.">choose</button> Tuesday’s class.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Leo finished assignment 2 and sent it through the official course portal before the deadline: He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="submitted" data-hint="Submit means deliver completed work through the required channel." data-fix="Leo submitted assignment 2 before the deadline.">choose</button> assignment 2.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Maya answered every question on the exam this morning, but the result will arrive tomorrow: She <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="took" data-hint="The exam happened, but the result is still unknown." data-fix="Maya took the exam this morning.">choose</button> the exam.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The course required 70 percent, and Leo’s final result was 82 percent: He <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="passed" data-hint="Leo met the stated required standard." data-fix="Leo passed the course with 82 percent.">choose</button> the course.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The tutor returned Maya’s draft with comments about its clear opening and missing example: Maya <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="received" data-hint="Comments about strengths and improvement are feedback." data-fix="Maya received feedback on her draft.">choose</button> feedback on her draft.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Separate study, learn, teach, practice, and review</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>verb</th><th>main viewpoint</th><th>natural example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">study</span></td><td>spend time examining a subject to learn it</td><td><span class="ex">I studied the vocabulary for thirty minutes.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">learn</span></td><td>develop knowledge or ability; it can be a process or result</td><td><span class="ex">I’m learning English. I learned five new terms.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">teach</span></td><td>help another person learn</td><td><span class="ex">The tutor taught us a repair phrase.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">practice</span></td><td>repeat an action to improve performance</td><td><span class="ex">We practiced giving short updates.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">review</span></td><td>look at learned material again</td><td><span class="ex">I reviewed my notes before class.</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p><span class="ex">Study</span> does not guarantee that learning happened, and <span class="ex">learn</span> is not limited to a completed result. Use the viewpoint supported by the context. With <span class="ex">teach</span>, use <span class="ex">teach someone something</span> or <span class="ex">teach something to someone</span>: <span class="ex">She taught us the pattern. She taught the pattern to us.</span></p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You selected teach, learn, study, practice, review, and ask from the learner’s or tutor’s precise purpose.">
    <h3>Drill 3: choose the learning action</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Learning action choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="teach">teach</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="learn">learn</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="study">study</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="practice">practice</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="review">review</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="ask">ask</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The tutor will help the group understand a new email pattern: She will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="teach" data-hint="The tutor gives guidance that helps the group learn." data-fix="The tutor will teach the group a new email pattern.">choose</button> the group a new email pattern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>By the end, Maya’s goal is to know and use ten new project words: She wants to <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="learn" data-hint="The goal is new knowledge and usable ability." data-fix="Maya wants to learn ten new project words.">choose</button> ten new project words.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Leo plans to spend thirty minutes examining the course notes tonight: He will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="study" data-hint="Study presents the time spent working with the subject matter." data-fix="Leo will study the course notes for thirty minutes.">choose</button> the course notes.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Maya will repeat the same one-minute update three times to improve fluency: She will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="practice" data-hint="Practice means repeat the performance in order to improve it." data-fix="Maya will practice the one-minute update three times.">choose</button> the one-minute update.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Before the quiz, Leo will look at last week’s notes again: He will <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="review" data-hint="Review means return to learned material." data-fix="Leo will review last week’s notes before the quiz.">choose</button> last week’s notes.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>Maya does not understand the final instruction, so she needs to request clarification: She should <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="ask" data-hint="The context requires a question to the tutor, not more guessing." data-fix="Maya should ask the tutor what the final instruction means.">choose</button> the tutor.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use evidence and ask for the exact help you need</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p><span class="ex">I studied a lot</span> reports effort. It does not by itself show progress. Useful evidence can compare a before-and-now sample, a stated score, the number of prompts needed, an action the learner can now complete, or specific feedback.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>broad message</th><th>more useful learning message</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">I’m better.</span></td><td><span class="ex">Last month I needed four prompts; today I needed one.</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">I don’t understand.</span></td><td><span class="ex">I understand the first step, but what does “compare the results” mean?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">What do I do?</span></td><td><span class="ex">Should I answer in writing or aloud?</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="ex">Where is it?</span></td><td><span class="ex">Where should I submit assignment 2?</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Other useful repair questions are <span class="ex">Could you repeat that more slowly? Could you give me another example? When is the assignment due?</span> A precise question lets the teacher repair the exact gap.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: stress the learning result and link the question</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">course</span> is /kɔrs/, <span class="ex">learn</span> is /lɝn/, <span class="ex">study</span> is /ˈstʌdi/, <span class="ex">education</span> is /ˌɛdʒəˈkeɪʃən/, <span class="ex">assignment</span> is /əˈsaɪnmənt/, and the noun <span class="ex">progress</span> is /ˈprɑɡrɛs/ in common U.S. speech.</p>
    <p>Stress the result or missing information: <span class="ex">I passed the <strong>COURSE</strong>. I need another <strong>EXAMPLE</strong>. Where should I submit the <strong>ASSIGNMENT</strong>?</span></p>
    <p>Keep the final sound in past actions: <span class="ex">studied</span> ends /d/, <span class="ex">practiced</span> ends /t/, and <span class="ex">completed</span> adds /ɪd/. In connected U.S. speech, <span class="ex">Could you</span> may begin /kʊdʒə/, and <span class="ex">Where should I</span> may sound like /wɛr ʃədaɪ/.</p>
    <p>Chunk the update by job: <span class="ex">My goal is clearer project updates | I attend class on Tuesdays | I needed four prompts before and one today | but I still need help with follow-up questions.</span></p>
  </div>

  <section data-lesson-extension="Tutor-read learning goal, course-class distinction, study action, progress evidence, feedback, and clarification check">
    <h2>Listen for the learning evidence</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p class="note-line"><b>Tutor-read listening:</b> Keep the transcript closed. Read each item once naturally and once after the learner chooses. The learner may use only the fictional Harbor details.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You heard the learning goal, scheduled class, study action, progress evidence, specific feedback, and precise clarification question.">
      <h3>Six learning-update decisions</h3>
      <div class="quiz-list">
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="give clearer project updates" data-hint="Listen for the ability the learner wants to improve after My goal is to." data-fix="The learning goal is to give clearer project updates."><p class="quiz-question">1. What is the learner’s goal?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="give clearer project updates">give clearer project updates</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="earn a science degree">earn a science degree</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="teach a math course">teach a math course</button></div></div>
        <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the Tuesday class at 6:00" data-hint="Listen for the day and time of the scheduled meeting." data-fix="The learner attends the Tuesday class at 6:00."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which scheduled meeting does the learner attend?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Tuesday class at 6:00">the Tuesday class at 6:00</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Thursday class at 8:00">the Thursday class at 8:00</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the Monday class at noon">the Monday class at noon</button></div></div>
