  <h2>Notice and repair imprecise education language</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="homeworks" data-hint="Homework is normally noncount; use a countable unit when the number matters." data-fix="Maya completed two homework assignments this week." data-why="Use homework without a plural ending. To count separate tasks, say two homework assignments." data-success-message="Correct. Homework is noncount, while assignment gives a countable task.">
    <h3>Drill 6: repair the countable unit</h3><p>Tap the word that incorrectly adds a plural ending to <span class="ex">homework</span>.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maya">Maya</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="completed">completed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="homeworks">homeworks</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="this-week">this week.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="learned" data-hint="The tutor helped the group acquire the skill, so use the giving side of the relationship." data-fix="The tutor taught us a useful repair phrase." data-why="Teach presents helping another person learn. The tutor taught us; the learners learned the phrase." data-success-message="Correct. The tutor taught the group, and the group learned the phrase.">
    <h3>Drill 7: repair the direction of learning</h3><p>Tap the verb that gives the learner’s role to the tutor.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the-tutor">The tutor</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="learned">learned</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="us">us</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="a-useful">a useful</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="repair-phrase">repair phrase.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="passed" data-hint="The learner completed the exam, but tomorrow’s result is still unknown." data-fix="Leo took the exam this morning, but the result will arrive tomorrow." data-why="Take an exam reports participation. Pass reports a successful result, which this context does not yet provide." data-success-message="Correct. Leo took the exam; the unknown result cannot yet show that he passed.">
    <h3>Drill 8: repair the unsupported result</h3><p>Results arrive tomorrow. Tap the verb that claims success too early.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="leo">Leo</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="passed">passed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="the-exam">the exam</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="this-morning">this morning,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="but-results">but results arrive tomorrow.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it without exposing private education records</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real school, employer, program, teacher, transcript, scores, grades, qualification, funding, disability, immigration status, schedule, or learning history. Use the fictional Harbor course. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Fictional learner card:</b> Goal: explain a project delay clearly; course: Business English 2; class: Tuesday at 6:00; routine: review model language and practice one update after each lesson.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Progress evidence:</b> First recording: five prompts. Today: two prompts and one follow-up answer without help. Keep the claim limited to this task.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Feedback and gap:</b> The timeline is clear, but the reason needs a more specific example. State what works before the remaining need.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Next step and repair:</b> Revise the reason, record again, and ask one precise question such as <span class="ex">Could you give me another example of a clear reason?</span></div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: give a 45–60 second fictional learning update</h3>
    <p>Use the Harbor card or another fictional adult course. Include the learning goal, subject or course, scheduled class, two study actions, one before-and-now comparison, one piece of feedback, a current gap, a next step, and one precise clarification question.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener distinguish effort from progress, identify what the learner can do now, and understand the exact support still needed?</p>
  </div>

